          {
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I found Microsoft documentation about **inventory status**, but not a live product catalog or a current list of items that are actually in stock. The docs explain that Microsoft Dynamics 365 Commerce can classify products as **in stock**, **low stock**, or **out of stock** based on inventory settings and thresholds.[ref_id:0][ref_id:3]\n\nThe retrieved content also says that:\n- inventory checks can be enabled before a product is added to the cart, and a product can be blocked from purchase if it is out of stock.[ref_id:0][ref_id:3]\n- inventory levels can be viewed for products in the Inventory Visibility app, where search results show the total quantity available in inventory.[ref_id:7]\n- stocked/inventoried products can be managed in Dynamics 365 Project Operations and Supply Chain scenarios.[ref_id:5][ref_id:6]\n\nIf you meant a specific Microsoft store, storefront, or product list, I’d need that source or product name to tell you which products are in stock.[ref_id:0][ref_id:7]"
              }
            ]
          }
